    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$R\\in R$ holds if and only if $R\\notin R$, a contradiction.\n\nEach possible membership status forces its opposite.",
      "worked": "Assume $R$ is a valid set.\n\nIf $R\\in R$, its defining condition requires $R\\notin R$, a contradiction.\n\nIf $R\\notin R$, it satisfies the defining condition for membership in $R$, so $R\\in R$, again a contradiction.\n\nBoth possibilities lead to a contradiction. Therefore $R$ is not a valid set.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
